                <pb facs="0802" n="714" sameAs="frus:frus1904/pg714"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. McCormick to Mr. Hay.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.—Paraphrase.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >American Embassy</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">St.
                                Petersburg</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1904-02-09"><hi rendition="#italic">February 9,
                        1904</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>(Mr. McCormick reports that the Russian Government has no objection to the
                    American representatives looking after the interests of Japan upon the
                    withdrawal of the Japanese diplomatic and consular representatives.)</p>
            </div>
        </body>
